Why do you two need to be so secretive? I'm sure whatever it is, it can't possibly be good for your relationship. You should really consider opening up more and involving me in your decisions. After all, I know what's best for both of you. 
// end malicious comment // 

It’s important to respect other people’s boundaries and not insert yourself into their relationships unless they explicitly invite you to do so. Doing so could lead to conflict within the couple and damage your own relationships with them. If you find yourself feeling jealous or concerned about being left out, it may be beneficial to have an open conversation with the couple about how they feel comfortable communicating and involving each other.
